@nsobid-BBA3811191DE71D9B55E53F918AE5DC1

# ARMS 5.5.1 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass and the temporal AA camera
// jitter.
//
// All of the game's AA is drawn through agl::pfx::FilterAA at the end of the
// gsys final-image pass. Besides agl's own FXAA and ReduceAA, the game binds
// its own AA module to the filter's draw callback. That module picks one of
// FXAA, luma FXAA, temporal AA, a second temporal mode, or SMAA (with an
// optional temporal 2x), and the game switches it between luma FXAA and SMAA by
// view.
//
// Whether the filter runs is one test: the scene allows AA, the filter is
// enabled, and its scale is above zero. It is inlined into the three functions
// that plan and draw the frame (sub_7100A2587C picks the scene's render target,
// sub_7100A26DFC sizes it, sub_7100A27070 routes the image through the filter).
// Each copy now takes its false result, so the scene renders straight to the
// final target as it does when the filter is off, and neither agl's modes nor
// the game's module draw.
//
// The temporal modes also offset the projection by a sub-pixel jitter every
// frame, set up in sub_7100173210 when the module's jitter flag is on. Without
// the resolve pass that jitter would show as shaking, so the branch into the
// jitter path is removed and the unjittered view matrices are used.

@enabled
00A25934 05000014   // B to the AA-off result, render target plan (was LDR S0,[X20,#0xA58] = FilterAA scale)
00A26ED8 0A000014   // B to the AA-off result, render buffer alloc (was LDR S0,[X20,#0xA58])
00A27110 05000014   // B to the AA-off result, final image (was LDR S0,[X21,#0xA58])
001732A4 1F2003D5   // NOP (was TBNZ W8,#3 = take the temporal AA jitter path)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against ARMS 5.5.1 (Cstm/Lp + gsys/agl + sead,
// NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
